diff --git a/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/03-disc-1-scratch-leaks-into-tmp.txt b/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/03-disc-1-scratch-leaks-into-tmp.txt
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/03-disc-1-scratch-leaks-into-tmp.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+VERSION: 1
+COMPONENTS: test_writing_support/python
+
+disc-1  SCRATCH DIRECTORIES LEAK INTO THE MACHINE'S /tmp      ** CLOSED **
+______________________________________________________________________________
+
+OBSERVED (2026-08-30): '/tmp' fills with 'vut_ids_*', 'vut_mutex_*',
+'vut_multi_*', 'vut_store_*', 'vut_provider_*' -- 108 of them after
+one afternoon's sweeps on the author's machine.
+
+WHERE THEY COME FROM. 33 test applications call 'tempfile.mkdtemp'
+(prefixes 'vut_prov_', 'vut_acc_', 'vut_eq_', 'vut_cov_', 'vut_walk_',
+... and the five above). The removal is not guaranteed:
+
+    test-directory-mutex.py     mkdtemp 1, rmtree 0
+    test-provider.py            mkdtemp 1, rmtree 0
+    test-stream_store.py        mkdtemp 1, rmtree 0
+    test-multi-execute.py       mkdtemp 1, rmtree 1, no 'finally'
+    test-test_id_db.py          rmtree at the END of each choice: a
+                                choice killed by the supervisor (the
+                                seven of disc-6 r-2) leaves every one
+
+Two causes, then: tests that never remove, and tests that remove only
+on the happy path -- and the interactive runner keeps the process
+alive across choices, so an 'atexit' would fire only at the session's
+end, and a kill never lets it fire at all.
+
+THE FIX THAT WAS TRIED AND TAKEN BACK. Launch every test process with
+'TMPDIR=<test dir>/TMP/scratch', so that whatever 'tempfile' makes
+lands under the transient root and 'rm -rf TMP/' -- or 'hwut.sanitize
+--transient' -- clears it. Built, run, reverted in the same pass:
+
+  -  it is a BEHAVIOUR CHANGE, and bookkeeper todo-1 ruled pass A
+     'no behaviour changes, wide, mechanical';
+  -  a fixture tree made under 'TMP/scratch' stands INSIDE the
+     project's tree, and its climb finds the project's own
+     'hwut-root.conf' -- so 'test-tree.py root' ("RootConfMissing,
+     as owed") stopped being owed, and every fixture reading that
+     relied on standing outside any tree derived a language it never
+     had. Fixtures that want a boundary already write one
+     ('script_runner.tree_boundary'); fixtures that want NONE have no
+     way to say so once '/tmp' is inside the tree.
+
+RECOMMENDATION, two parts, one ruling:
+
+  1  'script_runner.scratch(prefix)' -- ONE way to make a scratch
+     directory in a test: registers the path with the reference runner,
+     which removes every registered path when the CHOICE ends, happy
+     path or exception, and at process exit for what is left. The 33
+     call sites become one call each. A kill still leaks, and that is
+     honest: a killed process cannot clean.
+
+  2  The runner's scratch ground is '<test dir>/TMP/scratch' by
+     DEFAULT, with 'scratch(prefix, outside=True)' for the handful of
+     tests that must stand outside any tree ('test-tree.py root'). The
+     leak of a killed process then lands where '--transient' clears it,
+     and the machine's '/tmp' sees nothing of this project.
+
+     Part 2 is the behaviour change; it is the runner's (test-writing
+     support), not the framework's, and reaches the framework's own
+     suites only. Ruled together with part 1 or after it.
+
+CLOSED (2026-08-30, E-27, R-76). Part 2 was ruled and built: the
+procsitter exports 'TEST/TMP/scratch/<call>' as TMPDIR and lists what
+the call left ('created_tuple'); the climb ends at 'TEST/TMP', so a
+fixture built there stands outside every tree. Part 1 -- one
+'scratch()' in the runner that removes at the choice's end -- is
+still worth having and is not built; it is now a tidiness, not a
+leak.
diff --git a/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/04-todo-1-judgement-timing.txt b/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/04-todo-1-judgement-timing.txt
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/04-todo-1-judgement-timing.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+VERSION: 1
+COMPONENTS: engine/operations
+
+todo-1  WHEN A SUBJECT MAY BE JUDGED -- and what may abort a run
+        decided, unbuilt
+
+DECIDED (ruled in session)
+
+    '<hwut-end>' ends every test run: without a choice, with a
+    choice, interactive -- every road. (The session-path omission in
+    hwut_runner.__run_into_sinks is FIXED; see the R-70 fix note.)
+
+    STDOUT is an append-only stream. It may be compared WHILE it
+    arrives, line by line, against the nominal. A divergence there
+    MAY ABORT the run early.
+
+    A FILE develops with REVISIONS during the run -- written,
+    rewritten, truncated, seeked. Only its FINAL state is the
+    subject. It is judged only AFTER '<hwut-end>' has been received.
+    A file divergence can NEVER abort a run early.
+
+    THE COMPARATOR SETUP MUST BE CONDITIONED on the subject's kind:
+
+        comparator(stdout)   armed at run start; may stream;
+                             may abort the run
+        comparator(file)     armed at token receipt; judges the
+                             final state, once
+
+WHAT STANDS, WHAT DOES NOT
+
+    single run    files read after the end, judged after -- CONFORMS
+                  (stage_execute._output_files, R-71).
+    session       BUILT (this session): 'read_declared_files' is ONE
+                  implementation in stage_execute.py, called by both
+                  roads; the session calls it after the CHOICE'S
+                  'done' (which the token precedes), read-and-remove
+                  PER CHOICE. Containment speaks before a missing
+                  file. Proven: test-multi-execute.py--files (writer,
+                  forgetter, and an untouched file-less sibling).
+    early abort   NOT built on any road. All comparison happens
+                  after the run today.
+
+RULED -- file naming needs no new law
+    (source-file, choice) is unique by construction; 'test--choice'
+    extended by the output name stays unique AND parseable, provided
+    an output name never starts with '-'. That one refusal stands in
+    the validator (exploration, R-71); nothing else was needed.
+
+OPEN -- raise before building the early abort
+    (1) STREAMABILITY. Live judgement is only SOUND where a
+        divergence in a prefix implies divergence of the whole --
+        the comparison must be PREFIX-MONOTONE. Per-element
+        tolerances (numeric, eq-pattern on a line) are prefix-safe.
+        ANALOGY regions absorb REORDERING: the candidate's early
+        lines may match the nominal's late ones, so no prefix
+        verdict exists. A PYPE is an arbitrary filter: a sorting
+        pype makes the whole stream non-streamable. So the
+        comparator conditioning has a THIRD axis beside channel/file:
+
+            streamable      no pype, no analogy region in T
+                            -> live comparison, MAY abort
+            not streamable  -> judged whole, after the token,
+                            like a file
+
+        The conservative predicate costs nothing: where unsure,
+        judge after the token -- correctness never depends on the
+        abort, only speed does.
+
+    (2) RULED (standing, replayed): when a run is aborted, THE
+        ENTITY THAT TRIGGERS THE ABORT PROVIDES THE VERDICT -- FAIL
+        upon abortion. Any output content is IRRELEVANT: nothing is
+        recorded, nothing is kept, no candidate exists. Consistent
+        with the token law by construction: a stream without its
+        terminal token could never be promoted anyway.
diff --git a/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/05-todo-1-tree-model.txt b/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/05-todo-1-tree-model.txt
