@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+VERSION: 1
+COMPONENTS: services
+
+todo-1  hwut.renovate  (R-70 Q5; ruled, unbuilt)
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+services/renovate.py per the naming law. 'hwut.renovate
+--directory=X [--apply]'. Aspects, each reported; under --apply:
+
+    r-a  CONFIG IN HEADER: hwut 1.0 applications answering
+         '--hwut-info' with no in-file header -> REPORT (rewriting is
+         interview-based header generation; report-only first cut).
+    r-b  TERMINAL IN NOMINAL: GOODs not ending in '<hwut-end>' ->
+         APPEND under --apply. Beside it the advisory: pype-d tests
+         need the pype's '<eof>' emission, plain tests the app's own
+         (or the renovated HwutRunner). RULED (7a): --apply rewrites
+         GOODs only -- a tool must not edit an author's program;
+         scripts are report-only.
+
+RULED (chat, 2026-08-26): r-a IS PROMOTED FROM REPORT-ONLY TO A
+GENERATOR. 'hwut.renovate' takes the '--hwut-info' answer and WRITES A
+HEADER CONFIGURATION into the test application's own source.
+
+    hwut.renovate --directory=X [--apply]
+
+    for every candidate that answers '--hwut-info' and carries no
+    'hwut {' trigger:
+
+        interview it              (hwut_info_interview.interview)
+        render the answer as a header
+        insert it into the source, in that language's comment form
+
+    'The title;'  ->  title = "The title"
+    'CHOICES: a, b;'          ->  choices = ["a", "b"]
+    'HAPPY: <pattern>;' (0..n)->  happy   = [...]         (R-12: the
+                                  key is 'eq_pattern'; 'happy' was its
+                                  1.0 name)
+    'SAME;'                   ->  same        = true      (R-45)
+    'INTERACTIVE;'            ->  interactive = true      (R-46)
+
+WHY IT IS WORTH BUILDING. The interview is a MIGRATION PATH and it
+COSTS A PROCESS PER CANDIDATE, every exploration, for ever. A header
+is read from text. Renovating turns a permanent running cost into a
+one-time edit, and turns a specification the framework must ASK FOR
+into one it can READ.
+
+THIS BREAKS THE 7a RULING and does so knowingly: 7a says '--apply'
+rewrites GOODs only, because 'a tool must not edit an author's
+program'. Header generation edits the program. The distinction that
+justifies it: the header states WHAT THE PROGRAM ALREADY SAYS about
+itself, verbatim, and changes no behaviour -- it moves a statement
+from runtime to source. It is still an edit, so:
+
+  -  '--apply' is required; the default REPORTS the header it would
+     write, so the author reads it before it lands.
+  -  the insertion point and comment form are the language's, and a
+     language whose comment form is not known is REPORTED, never
+     guessed at.
+  -  a file already carrying a trigger is never touched.
+
+OPEN, one ruling before building:
+
+    Does the generated header REPLACE the '--hwut-info' block in the
+    source, or stand beside it?
+
+    RECOMMENDED: STAND BESIDE IT, untouched. The block is executable
+    code that may do more than print (a 1.0 application often exits
+    on it), and deleting code is a different act from adding a
+    comment. The header wins by precedence anyway -- HEADER outranks
+    INTERVIEW (R-44) -- so the block becomes dead weight the author
+    may remove at leisure, and the renovation stays reversible by
+    deleting the lines it added.
+
+
+RULED (chat, 2026-08-27): THE RENOVATOR MUST ENTER THE BOOKS, much as
+'hwut.accept' does.
+
+A renovated test application is READ by the framework -- the header
+carries its title and choices -- but the BOOK still knows nothing of
+it. And exploration is only half the story: what a face asks the book
+for ('hwut.report', 'hwut.stability', a stain, a run id) is absent for
+every test that has never been accepted, so a renovated tree answers
+'never run' to every question about its own history.
+
+So renovation writes what an acceptance would have written:
+
+    THE BOOK       'GOOD/result_db.json': an entry per (test, choice)
+                   -- the configuration it was read under, the choices
+                   it declares.
+    THE REGISTER   'GOOD/test_ids.dat': an id per application and per
+                   choice, born as 'hwut.accept' bears them (B-2: ids
+                   issued once, never reused).
+
+WHAT IT DOES NOT WRITE: a NOMINAL. A blessed artefact is the author's
+act and a migration has no standing to perform it -- the 1.0 GOOD
+files are already there, under the 1.0 naming, and whether the
+framework learns that naming or the files are moved is E-14's open
+question, not the renovator's to settle.
+
+NOR A VERDICT. The book entry says 'this test exists and is
+configured thus', never 'this test passed'. A renovator has run
+nothing.
+
+OPEN: whether the entry is written under '--apply' only, as r-a and
+r-b are, or whether entering the books is harmless enough to be the
+default. RECOMMENDED: '--apply', like the rest -- a file under
+'GOOD/' is the framework's memory, and writing it unasked is the same
+class of act as rewriting a header.
diff --git a/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/0s-todo-2-command-line-completion.txt b/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/0s-todo-2-command-line-completion.txt
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/0s-todo-2-command-line-completion.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+VERSION: 1
+COMPONENTS: services
+
+todo-2-command-line-completion.txt                    ** DESIGN, NOT BUILT **
+______________________________________________________________________________
+
+RAISED (chat, 2026-08-29). Every face should complete on TAB, in bash,
+zsh and PowerShell at least.
+
+==============================================================================
+THE CONSTRAINT THAT DECIDES THE DESIGN
+==============================================================================
+MEASURED, on the machine this was written on:
+
+    import vut.services.run          0.711 s
+
+A COMPLETION RUNS ON EVERY TAB PRESS. Seven hundred milliseconds is a
+terminal that feels broken, and a person will stop pressing TAB rather
+than wait. So the design is not 'where does the completion logic go' —
+it is 'HOW LITTLE CAN BE LOADED BEFORE ANSWERING'.
+
+==============================================================================
+THE SHAPE
+==============================================================================
+ONE ENTRY, on the general face:
+
+    hwut --command-line-complete <shell-name> "<the line so far>"
+
+AND IT IS ANSWERED BEFORE ANYTHING IS IMPORTED. The launcher's module
+opens:
+
+    import sys
+    if "--command-line-complete" in sys.argv[1:3]:
+        from vut.services import _complete
+        sys.exit(_complete.main(sys.argv[2:]))
+    #  everything else -- the engine, the orchestrator, compare --
+    #  is imported BELOW this line and never reached on a TAB.
+
+'_complete' imports 'os', 're' and nothing of this tree. THE FAST PATH
+IS THE WHOLE POINT: a completion that loads the engine has already
+lost, whatever else it gets right.
+
+THE SHELL NAME IS AN ARGUMENT because the three shells want different
+things: bash wants bare lines, zsh wants 'candidate:description'
+pairs, PowerShell wants its own object shape. ONE COMPLETER, three
+renderings — and adding a shell is a rendering, not a reimplementation.
+
+THE WHOLE LINE IS PASSED, not a word index. The completer parses it
+itself, so the shell scripts stay thin enough to be obviously correct,
+and a bug is fixed in Python rather than in three dialects of shell.
+
+==============================================================================
+THREE TIERS, AND ONLY THE FIRST IS FREE
+==============================================================================
+    STATIC     the face names, the option names of each face
+               NO TREE READ AT ALL. A table in '_complete', or the
+               'USAGE_TOKEN_TUPLE' of the wish -- but read as TEXT,
+               never by importing the module that holds it.
+
+    CHEAP      test applications here, choices of one, directories
+               ONE DIRECTORY LISTING, or one file read. 'hwut.play
+               <TAB>' offering the applications of this directory
+               costs an 'os.listdir' and a line scan for the marker.
+
+    DEAR       labels that stand, targets that are bound
+               THE FILE MUST BE READ AND PARSED. 'hwut-root.labels'
+               is small and its format is simple, so a private reader
+               in '_complete' is right -- IMPORTING 'labels/_file.py'
+               DRAGS THE ENGINE IN, and that is the trade this whole
+               design exists to refuse.
+
+    WHERE A TIER CANNOT BE ANSWERED CHEAPLY, IT ANSWERS NOTHING. A
+    completion that is sometimes absent is a small disappointment; one
+    that is always slow is abandoned.
+
+==============================================================================
+THE LAW A COMPLETER MUST NEVER BREAK
+==============================================================================
+IT NEVER FAILS LOUDLY. A traceback printed into a shell's completion
+buffer corrupts what the person was typing. Every path in '_complete'
+that could raise ends in 'no candidates', silently -- this is the ONE
+place in this framework where swallowing is correct, and it is correct
+for the same reason the observer swallows (operations/observer.py): a
+watcher must not break what it watches.
+
+IT WRITES NOTHING AND RUNS NOTHING. No lock is taken, no file is
+created, no test is executed. A TAB is not a command.
+
+==============================================================================
+WHAT WOULD BE COMPLETED
+==============================================================================
+    hwut.<TAB>                    the face names
+    hwut.run --<TAB>              the wish's options, and run's own
+    hwut.run --label <TAB>        the labels that stand          DEAR
+    hwut.play <TAB>               the applications here          CHEAP
+    hwut.play test-a.sh <TAB>     that application's choices     CHEAP
+    hwut.target <TAB>             the targets bound here         DEAR
+    hwut.labels.remove <TAB>      the labels that stand          DEAR
+    --dir <TAB>                   directories below here         CHEAP
+
+==============================================================================
+OPEN
+==============================================================================
+ a  DOES THE GENERAL FACE ANSWER FOR ALL, or does each face answer
+    for itself? One entry means one fast path to keep fast; per-face
+    means each knows its own options without a table.
+    RECOMMENDED: THE GENERAL FACE, with the per-face option lists
+    read from a TABLE in '_complete'. A table duplicates what the
+    faces declare -- but the alternative imports them, and that is
+    the 0.711 s this design exists to avoid. THE TABLE'S DRIFT IS
+    CATCHABLE: a suite can compare it against each face's real
+    'USAGE_TOKEN_TUPLE' and go red when they part.
+
+ b  IS THERE A COMPLETION FOR '<file-glob>'? The short form takes
+    bare words as targets, and a person may want the applications
+    offered there too.
+    RECOMMENDED: yes, same CHEAP tier as 'hwut.play'.
+______________________________________________________________________________
diff --git a/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/0t-disc-1-test-sequence-form.txt b/vut/adm/WORK/gathered/0t-disc-1-test-sequence-form.txt
new file mode 100644
